Keep the columns' docs in every schema the extension writes.

ALTER TABLE's ADD, DROP and RENAME COLUMN, and a change of a column's
type, copy the table's current schema, change one column and commit the
copy as a new schema. The copy kept each field's doc, the column's
comment, but neither writer of a schema's JSON wrote it: the copy that
goes into the add-schema update (AddNamedField) and the update itself as
it is sent to the catalog (AddStructField). So a change to one column
dropped the comments of every column of the table, and apps that keep
tags in column comments lost all of a table's tags with any change to its
columns. Both now write a field's doc, nested fields' included.

diff --git a/src/catalog/rest/api/iceberg_create_table_request.cpp b/src/catalog/rest/api/iceberg_create_table_request.cpp
index 2484293..391da53 100644
--- a/src/catalog/rest/api/iceberg_create_table_request.cpp
+++ b/src/catalog/rest/api/iceberg_create_table_request.cpp
@@ -130,6 +130,12 @@ static void AddUnnamedField(yyjson_mut_doc *doc, yyjson_mut_val *field_obj, cons
 static void AddNamedField(yyjson_mut_doc *doc, yyjson_mut_val *field_obj, const IcebergColumnDefinition &column) {
 	yyjson_mut_obj_add_strcpy(doc, field_obj, "name", column.name.c_str());
 	yyjson_mut_obj_add_uint(doc, field_obj, "id", column.id);
+	//! Igloo: a field keeps its doc, the column's comment. Every new schema (ADD, DROP and RENAME COLUMN, a change
+	//! of type) is the current one copied through here, so without it a change to one column dropped the comments
+	//! of every column.
+	if (!column.doc.empty()) {
+		yyjson_mut_obj_add_strncpy(doc, field_obj, "doc", column.doc.c_str(), column.doc.size());
+	}
 	if (column.type.id() != LogicalTypeId::VARIANT && column.type.IsNested()) {
 		auto type_obj = yyjson_mut_obj_add_obj(doc, field_obj, "type");
 		AddUnnamedField(doc, type_obj, column);
